challenge_solution:
Place <button id="reset" type="button">Reset</button> before the script, then add this inside the existing script after the greeting listener.

```javascript
document.querySelector("#reset").addEventListener("click", () => {
  document.querySelector("#name").value = "";
  document.querySelector("#result").textContent = "";
});
```

Test by greeting Fav, clicking Reset and confirming both fields clear. A required attribute only guides this browser interaction. A caller can construct another request, so the server still has to verify who owns the record.
